From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:48:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 380/443] [ae-patch] Fix the voice log upload, add a Level
 meter setting, and show the approval on the voice sheet (0380)

The voice log upload no longer uses keepalive from an open page (iOS WebKit drops it): in-page uploads are plain requests with a 10 s timeout, so a hung request can no longer leave every later automatic upload throttled. Keepalive is used only when the page is hidden or closing, and a rejected keepalive request is retried once without it. Every upload result lands in the log buffer and a Voice-end result is toasted. A release no longer lets a synchronous stop upload mic_failed at chat creation.
A per-device Level meter setting in the speaker menu and the new-chat Voice menu. It is off by default on iPhone and Safari, where the meter's second microphone capture can take the mic from the recognizer; with it off, the ring and bars follow the recognizer's events and the stall check uses them too.
While a voice-answerable approval is pending, the Voice panel shows Waiting for your OK with Run it and Decline buttons in every phase, including while the line plays. Every client caller of an approval now passes _meta.source, and the resolve route logs one INFO line with the session, elicitation, action and an allowlisted source.
